# Single source of truth for browser targets, shared by eslint-plugin-compat and any
# future syntax transpilation.
#
# The SDK's real floor is not `defaults` but the Web Crypto APIs it depends on, for which
# no polyfill exists: `crypto.subtle` (PKCE code challenge, One Tap nonce) and
# `crypto.randomUUID` (correlation id). That puts the honest minimum at early 2022 —
# IE11 was never actually supported, despite Babel having targeted it until now.
defaults
not dead
